# sent_id = S000171
# speaker = Scrofa
# edition_loc = 1.6.1
# text_old = Formae cum duo genera sint, una quam natura dat, altera quam sationes imponunt, prior, quod alius ager bene natus, alius male, posterior, quod alius fundus bene consitus est, alius male, dicam prius de naturali.
# text = formae cum duo genera sint, una quam natura dat, altera quam sationes imponunt, prior, quod alius ager bene natus, alius male, posterior, quod alius fundus bene consitus est, alius male, dicam prius de naturali.
# text_en = As shapes are of two kinds — one which nature gives, the other which planting imposes (the former in that one field is naturally good, another bad; the latter in that one estate is well planted, another badly) — I will speak first about the natural kind.
# text_fr = Comme les formes sont de deux genres — l’une que la nature donne, l’autre qu’imposent les plantations (la première en ce qu’un champ est bien né, un autre mal ; la seconde en ce qu’un domaine est bien planté, un autre mal) — je parlerai d’abord de la [forme] naturelle.
# text_fi = Kun muodot ovat kahta lajia — toinen, jonka luonto antaa, toinen, jonka istutukset asettavat (edellinen siina, etta yksi pelto on luonnostaan hyva, toinen huono; jalkimmainen siina, etta yksi tila on hyvin istutettu, toinen huonosti) — puhun ensin luonnollisesta [muodosta].
# review_status = silver
# elevated_from = bronze
